title: Haul Away, Joe
artist: Traditional
origin: England
culture: English
genre: Sea shanty
language: en
key: D minor
tempo: 76
meter: 2/4
pickup: 0
intro: 2
outro: 1
style: shanty
guide: ooh
year: 1914
attribution: Anonymous 19th-century short-haul shanty, printed in Cecil Sharp's English Folk-Chanteys (1914) and in R. R. Terry's The Shanty Book (1921), which has both the "little boy" verse and the "haul for better weather" line used here. Traditional melody and words, public domain worldwide.
source_url: https://abcnotation.com/tunePage?a=dmc.lizmilner.com/viewabc.vbhtml%3Ffile=Haul+Away+Joe/0002
tags: sea shanty, sailor, singalong, minor, work song
# One verse (16 bars of 2/4) and the chorus (8 bars). Source is in E minor; transposed to D minor.

